;; Frame registrations are the operator's per research-plan-v1 §11.
;; ALL FIELDS NOW SET. The five fields the first draft marked CONFIRM were
;; conventions, not decisions -- round constants or computations -- and were
;; derived (Joe, 2026-08-18: "if it is a convention to ask me something, please
;; think about how that can be avoided"). The one genuine decision, plan §6's
;; fresh-per-N wording, was RULED on 2026-08-18: fresh per N, N = 2.
;;
;; f9 is the FIRST of this Analyst's two frames; f10 is the second and last.
;; Succession follows f10.

;;
;; Purpose: first frame with an ANALYST SEAT in the loop, and the first frame
;; in which the memory cascade runs and is receipted.
;;
;; Problem selection — a01J06. Criteria, each verified rather than inherited:
;;   * OPEN AT THE PIN, verified by elaboration, not by metadata. `lake env lean`
;;     under the pinned project exits 0 and emits exactly one
;;     `declaration uses `sorry`` diagnostic in a 174-line Main.lean. This
;;     matters: on 2026-08-18 a corpus audit found `status.json` wrong for 139
;;     of 443 bundles, INCLUDING the previously-favoured f9 candidate a02J03,
;;     which declares 3 sorries and in fact elaborates clean with none. Frame
;;     selection must require a fresh elaboration; the label is a hypothesis.
;;     (futon3c holes/excursions/E-apm-bundle-sorry-drift.md; apm-lean 6062223.)
;;   * a-family, as f8 was. Frame-2 chose family distance to limit cross-problem
;;     recall leakage; that is NOT satisfied here and is a KNOWN DEPARTURE — see
;;     :reg/known-departures.
;;   * TOUCHES AN EDGED PATTERN, so the cascade's :why-hop route can fire rather
;;     than every offer being :leaf. This is the point of running f9 at all.
;;
;; Prior exposure — DECLARED, not hidden. Operator ruling 2026-08-18: prior work
;; surfacing on a related problem is "a test of the system working much as
;; designed", not leakage; leakage would be deliberately mining a solution in
;; for this frame. The exposure is one reviewed :feedback memory deposited by
;; M-codex-sorry-loop in the ordinary course of its work:
;;   e-codexpilot-preflight-domain-guards-and-inferred-bound-types-in-analysis-statements
;;   attached to math-strategy/corpus-trust-protocol
;;             and math-formalization/notation-semantics-traps
;;   naming problems a02J03, a02J07, a92J07, a93A02.
;; a01J06 is NOT itself named in that memory, so the exposure reaches it only
;; structurally — via the patterns — which is exactly the channel f9 measures.
;;
;; THE ANALYST HANDOFF PATTERN (Joe asked; recording it here so the frame does
;; not depend on anyone remembering it):
;;   The Analyst wakes ONCE, AT CLOSE, and never mid-frame. futon3c
;;   apm/conductor.clj `close!` sends exactly one completion bell to the seat
;;   named by :analyst-seat (or FUTON3C_APM_ANALYST_SEAT) after a terminal close
;;   succeeds; an incomplete or thrown close does not wake it, and a missing or
;;   off-roster seat is reported as :skipped without breaking close. The payload
;;   carries problem id, cycle id, :launchable? and a failure count — enough to
;;   begin without reconstructing context. Built and reviewed 2026-08-17
;;   (futon3c b27bccf7). On waking the Analyst performs duties A, B and F:
;;   transfer checks + series entry, an S reading, and divergence -> small belled
;;   packet -> park -> personal review at the gate -> merge -> register the
;;   hypothesis the fix implies. It does NOT touch a frame in flight.

